.TH LT-QWWAD_TX_DOUBLE_BARRIER_IV "1" "September 2016" "lt-qwwad_tx_double_barrier_iv (Quantum Wells, Wires and Dots) 1.5.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lt-qwwad_tx_double_barrier_iv \- compute current--voltage characteristics for a double tunnelling barrier.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lt-qwwad_tx_double_barrier_iv
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Find the current through a double barrier structure as a function of bias voltage.
.SH OPTIONS

Generic options:
.TP
\fB\-h\fR [ \fB\-\-help\fR ]
display a help message
.TP
\fB\-v\fR [ \fB\-\-version\fR ]
display the version of the program
.HP
\fB\-c\fR [ \fB\-\-config\fR ] arg (=qwwad.cfg) name of the configuration file to be used
.SS "Program-specific options:"
.TP
\fB\-l\fR [ \fB\-\-leftbarrierwidth\fR ] arg (=100)
Width of left barrier [angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-b\fR [ \fB\-\-wellwidth\fR ] arg (=100)
Width of well [angstrom].
.HP
\fB\-r\fR [ \fB\-\-rightbarrierwidth\fR ] arg (=100) Width of right barrier [angstrom].
.TP
\fB\-m\fR [ \fB\-\-wellmass\fR ] arg (=0.067)
Effective mass in well (relative to
that of a free electron). This is used
to compute the distribution of carriers
at the input.
.TP
\fB\-n\fR [ \fB\-\-barriermass\fR ] arg (=0.067)
Effective mass in barrier (relative to
that of a free electron).
.TP
\fB\-\-barrierpotential\fR arg (=100)
Barrier potential [meV]
.TP
\fB\-\-Te\fR arg (=300)
Temperature of carrier distribution [K]
.TP
\fB\-d\fR [ \fB\-\-dE\fR ] arg (=0.01)
Energy step [meV]
.SS "Configuration options:"
.TP
\fB\-V\fR [ \fB\-\-verbose\fR ]
display lots of information about calculation
.SH FILES
.SS Output files:
  'IV.r'   Current--voltage characteristics:
           Column 1: voltage [V].
           Column 2: current [a.u.].
  'T.r'    Transmission coefficient as a function of energy:
           Column 1: energy of incident carrier [meV].
           Column 2: transmission coefficient.
.SH EXAMPLES
Compute current--voltage characteristics through a pair of 100-meV, 200-angstrom barriers separated by a 50-angstrom well at 50 K temperature:
   qwwad_tx_double_barrier_iv --leftbarrierwidth 200 --rightbarrierwidth 200 --barrierpotential 100 --wellwidth 50 --Te 50

Compute current--voltage characteristics through a pair of 1-eV, 100-angstrom barrier, with effective mass = 0.1 m0, using resolution of 1 meV:
   qwwad_tx_double_barrier_iv --barrierpotential 1000 --leftbarrierwidth 100 --rightbarrierwidth 100 --barriermass 0.1 --dE 1
